object, left:floor, right:wall} and adjacent_walkability={up:blocked, down:blocked, left:walkable, right:walkable}, i.e. LEFT is advertised as walkable - and the LEFT move silently fails because a sprite is standing there. The sprite layer shows it precisely: with the player at cell (4,3), a sprite sits at cell (3,3), directly left. So the agent is told a tile is free, tries it, and nothing happens with no explanation - the same silent-failure shape as the dialogue box and the door graphics. The two fields also contradict each other on RIGHT at that position (terrain label says 'wall', ROM collision says 'walkable'); the collision table was right in every move actually attempted, on both the moves that worked and the ones that were blocked, which is the 99.2%-vs-83.6% split showing up live. FIX: subtract occupied sprite cells from walkability before reporting it. The data is already being read for the sprite layer (wSpriteStateData1), so this is a join, not new RE/data work - and it retires the most confusing failure mode the agent has, because 'walkable but nothing happens' is indistinguishable from a broken bridge.", "depends_on": [], "created_at": "2026-09-28 20:38:42", "updated_at": "2026-09-28 20:40:16", "reasoning": "This is the difference between a reader that reports 'no exits' and one that reports 'no exits THAT I CAN SEE'. The first makes the agent walk into walls and the operator think the game is broken; the second is a fact the agent can plan around. Warps are cheap to read from the ROM and turn an invisible wall into a coordinate. It also retires a misleading suggested_action, which is worse than no suggestion because it gets followed.", "complexity": "small", "capability_tags": ["perception", "ram", "navigation", "warps", "rom"], "worker_status": "complete", "commit_hash": "bbffe0a", "completed_at": "2026-09-29T01:00:00-05:00", "guard_result": "4317 passed, 15 skipped; ruff clean; mypy clean", "ci_result": "success", "foreman_note": "Recovered wave merged; sprite occupancy now overrides ROM walkability."}
